{"question_id": "test_00038", "variant": "v0", "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash", "predicted_answer": "D", "explanation": "The therapeutic index is typically calculated as TD50/ED50. From the efficacy data, the ED50 (dose where 50% of patients improve) is approximately 20 mg (19/49 ≈ 39%, 30 mg 26/53 ≈ 49%, so ED50 ~ 30 mg). From the safety data, the TD50 (dose where 50% have adverse events) is between 60 mg (15/42 ≈ 36%) and 80 mg (23/47 ≈ 49%), so TD50 ~ 80 mg. Thus, therapeutic index ≈ 80/30 ≈ 2.67.", "confidence": 0.85, "gold_answer": "D", "is_correct": true, "total_latency_ms": 3663.194417953491, "total_token_usage": {"input": 321, "output": 156}, "estimated_cost": null, "evidence_used": null, "retrieval_latency_ms": null, "retrieval_token_usage": null, "iteration_count": null, "verifier_verdict": null, "verdict_history": null, "stopped_after_max_iterations": null, "reasoning_latency_ms": 3662.7862453460693, "reasoning_token_usage": {"input": 321, "output": 156}, "verifier_latency_ms": null, "verifier_token_usage": null, "query_rewrite_count": null, "rewriter_latency_ms": null, "rewriter_token_usage": null, "stm_scope_used": null, "loop_history_length": null, "ltm_facts_retrieved": null, "ltm_write_triggered": null, "user_id": null}
